      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "Okay. So now we know what API routes are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "that we can write server-side code there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 10.63,
          "en": "Node.js code to be specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.63,
          "end": 13.73,
          "en": "that we can handle different kinds of requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.73,
          "end": 15.17,
          "en": "that we can extract data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.17,
          "end": 19.05,
          "en": "and then run any kind of Node.js code we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.05,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "We can then also send back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 23.42,
          "en": "or different responses depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.42,
          "end": 25.76,
          "en": "on the kind of request sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.76,
          "end": 28.87,
          "en": "And so, for example, if I still enter a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.87,
          "end": 31.77,
          "en": "and send it to slash API slash feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.77,
          "end": 34.98,
          "en": "through the browser URL bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "that will automatically be a get request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "Therefore, it will not trigger this if block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 43.73,
          "en": "or it'll not make it into this if block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.73,
          "end": 46.67,
          "en": "because the method is not post, but get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.67,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "And therefore this line of code will execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 51.623,
          "en": "which is why we see this response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 54.49,
          "en": "And now that we got this response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.49,
          "end": 57.44,
          "en": "of course, let me also make it crystal clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.44,
          "end": 60.41,
          "en": "that you can also handle incoming get requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.41,
          "end": 62.14,
          "en": "in whichever way you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.14,
          "end": 66.26,
          "en": "So for example, here, let's say for incoming get requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.26,
          "end": 68.17,
          "en": "we wanna get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.17,
          "end": 73.16,
          "en": "to all our feedback objects that were stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.16,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "and return those as JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 78.47,
          "en": "So that in our front end application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.47,
          "end": 81.75,
          "en": "we could also send a behind the scenes request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 85.08,
          "en": "to fetch all feedback entries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 87.87,
          "en": "and display them on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 91.69,
          "en": "So to achieve this in our API feedback route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.69,
          "end": 93.97999999999999,
          "en": "I will basically repeat the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.97999999999999,
          "end": 97.34,
          "en": "from up there to get access to my file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.34,
          "end": 100.07,
          "en": "And hence we can copy that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.07,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "or, to avoid code duplication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 107.9,
          "en": "create helper functions like buildFeedbackPath, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 113.53,
          "en": "where I simply return this file path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.53,
          "end": 114.8,
          "en": "which I create here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.8,
          "end": 119.27000000000001,
          "en": "So where I return this, so that down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.27000000000001,
          "end": 122.173,
          "en": "we can just execute buildFeedbackPath,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.44,
          "end": 125.783,
          "en": "and then do this again here in the else block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.81,
          "end": 131.67,
          "en": "And also to then get our file data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.67,
          "end": 133.923,
          "en": "we can create another function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.96,
          "end": 140.12,
          "en": "extractFeedback could be the function name and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.12,
          "end": 144.667,
          "en": "in extractFeedback, I in the end wanna execute that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 149.94,
          "en": "so we can copy that code, move that in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.94,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "Expect the file path as a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 157.44299999999998,
          "en": "and then simply return the parsed data as a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.53,
          "end": 164.53,
          "en": "And then below here in that code, we can now get our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.65,
          "end": 168.89,
          "en": "by calling extract feedback and passing our file path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.89,
          "end": 170.57,
          "en": "as a argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.57,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "With that refactoring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 176.48,
          "en": "we can repeat that down here in the else block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.48,
          "end": 178.45,
          "en": "And then we got that extracted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.45,
          "end": 182.29,
          "en": "and parsed feedback data in that data constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.29,
          "end": 183.35,
          "en": "And hence, instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.35,
          "end": 186.83,
          "en": "of sending back this dummy, 'this works' message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.83,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "we could send back our feedback, our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 192.673,
          "en": "which we're extracting from the feedback file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.61,
          "end": 196.21,
          "en": "And if we do that and save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.21,
          "end": 199.74,
          "en": "if I now reload slash API slash feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.74,
          "end": 201.763,
          "en": "we see that this also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.63,
          "end": 206.3,
          "en": "But of course we typically don't add an API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.3,
          "end": 211.3,
          "en": "so that users have to enter them in their URL bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.75,
          "end": 215.47,
          "en": "That's not the user experience we typically wanna offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.47,
          "end": 218.8,
          "en": "Instead, maybe on local host slash 3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.8,
          "end": 220.75,
          "en": "we wanna have a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.75,
          "end": 225.75,
          "en": "that loads all the stored feedback items from that API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.16,
          "end": 230.05,
          "en": "or with help of that API route when it's clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.05,
          "end": 234.12,
          "en": "So on index.js, below the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.12,
          "end": 235.8,
          "en": "we'll add a horizontal line,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.8,
          "end": 238.87,
          "en": "and then a button where I say load feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.87,
          "end": 240.52,
          "en": "And when that button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.52,
          "end": 244.43,
          "en": "I wanna send a get request to my feedback API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.43,
          "end": 247.823,
          "en": "to trigger this else block and get that feedback data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.84,
          "end": 251.63,
          "en": "For this in the front end, in index.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.63,
          "end": 255.46,
          "en": "in my homepage component, I add another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.46,
          "end": 259.19,
          "en": "which should be triggered when this new button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.19,
          "end": 262.75,
          "en": "And that could be the load feedback handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.75,
          "end": 264.68,
          "en": "Name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.68,
          "end": 267.44,
          "en": "And in there I also want to send a fetch request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.44,
          "end": 269.75,
          "en": "to slash API feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.75,
          "end": 271.04,
          "en": "So I will actually copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.04,
          "end": 274.46,
          "en": "that code from up there and paste it in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.46,
          "end": 278.22,
          "en": "but I will not set this configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.22,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "because here I do wanna send a get request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 285.02,
          "en": "I have no extra data that should be added to the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.02,
          "end": 289.13,
          "en": "and I therefore also don't need to set any headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.13,
          "end": 291.58,
          "en": "So just sending a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.58,
          "end": 294.623,
          "en": "by just passing in the URL is enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 295.6,
          "end": 298.23,
          "en": "Now let's connect this loadFeedbackHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 298.23,
          "end": 299.7,
          "en": "to this button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.7,
          "end": 303.21,
          "en": "through the onClick prop loadFeedbackHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.29,
          "end": 309.2,
          "en": "And then we can of course do more useful things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.2,
          "end": 311.45,
          "en": "with our data here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.45,
          "end": 314.03,
          "en": "Currently, we're just logging it to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.03,
          "end": 315.66,
          "en": "We could also set some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.66,
          "end": 317.96,
          "en": "that renders the feedback items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.96,
          "end": 319.26,
          "en": "So let's maybe do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.26,
          "end": 322.31,
          "en": "Let's import useState from react,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.31,
          "end": 326.243,
          "en": "and let's register some state here by calling useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.22,
          "end": 329.53,
          "en": "And let's say initially we have an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.616,
          "end": 333.15,
          "en": "for our feedbackItems state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.15,
          "end": 337.1,
          "en": "And then a setFeedbackItems updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.1,
          "end": 338.24,
          "en": "So that could be state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.24,
          "end": 340.76,
          "en": "which we now use in the homepage component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 340.76,
          "end": 343.38,
          "en": "And now I wanna set my state whenever I did",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 343.38,
          "end": 345.4,
          "en": "fetch my feedback data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 345.4,
          "end": 348.40999999999997,
          "en": "So then here in the loadFeedbackHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.40999999999997,
          "end": 350.99,
          "en": "instead of logging the feedback to the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.99,
          "end": 355.76,
          "en": "I'll call setFeedbackItems to update that feedback state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.76,
          "end": 359.46,
          "en": "And I want to update it with that data that was fetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 359.46,
          "end": 361.96,
          "en": "Now, keep in mind that the data we're sending back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 361.96,
          "end": 364.62,
          "en": "will be an object with a feedback property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 364.62,
          "end": 367.17,
          "en": "which holds the actual data parsed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 367.17,
          "end": 369.05,
          "en": "from the feedback JSON file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.05,
          "end": 371.6,
          "en": "And therefore it's this feedback property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 371.6,
          "end": 372.69,
          "en": "which will give us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.69,
          "end": 376.06,
          "en": "to that feedback array stored in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 376.06,
          "end": 379.57,
          "en": "Hence, when we work with our response data on the front end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 379.57,
          "end": 384,
          "en": "we want to set data.feedback as our feedback items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384,
          "end": 387.64,
          "en": "because that is then accessing that feedback property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 387.64,
          "end": 390.88,
          "en": "which is being set on the response and which therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 390.88,
          "end": 394.223,
          "en": "does hold those feedback items in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.7,
          "end": 397.44,
          "en": "And now we're setting that state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.44,
          "end": 400.62,
          "en": "and we can now use that state in our homepage component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 400.62,
          "end": 404.38,
          "en": "below the button to simply output an unordered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 404.38,
          "end": 408.24,
          "en": "of feedback items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 408.24,
          "end": 413.24,
          "en": "which we map to list items where I then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 413.55,
          "end": 418.55,
          "en": "simply output item.text, because my feedback items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.04,
          "end": 423.22,
          "en": "as stored in feedback.json do have a text property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 423.22,
          "end": 426.11,
          "en": "and these are the items we're working with here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 426.11,
          "end": 428.33,
          "en": "So we can output the text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 428.33,
          "end": 430.43,
          "en": "And since we're mapping, also set a key",
          "zh": ""
        },
